Some armors (mithril, many cloaks) actually do protect from various special 
attacks including level drains. The protection is not 100%, but is good enough
(99.33%). So if you are wearing e.g. a clak of magic resistance - go ahead with
the Tsurugi, even if you happen to lose one level - you'll immediately
recover it in your next kill.

GDSM provides btw. some protection from level drain, but is not that good.

The real reason why I often wield Excalibur instead of ToM is that I want to
keep that polished shield in the other hand...
